Purpose:
  Phase 4 calibrated semantic GPS gameplay surface for movement, Map readiness, status, rewards, and Cell inspection through inspect-map-cell. Its static native fog legend is exactly Shrouded, Informed, Explored, and Present: Present is clearest and highest contrast, Explored is remembered at lower contrast, Informed is reachable and known but visibly not Explored, and Shrouded is most concealed. These treatments remain static, grayscale-safe, and never depend on hue alone; Shrouded exposes no detail. The current player center marker remains visible for trusted, low-confidence, and paused states, with one additive trust or eligibility ring rather than a second marker. Present requires trusted physical occupancy; the paused banner remains a semantic status; legacy hasLoot never adds a star; rarity, loot, and warm-hue semantics are not Fog state. Organic geometry provenance, coordinates, rings, polygons, counts, source metadata, frontier edge and seam behavior, MapLibre, projections, painters, routes, FogStateService, providers, data/schema, visits, eligibility, marker interpolation, and gestures remain unchanged. Phase 4 calibrates renderer hierarchy only: it authorizes neither Phase 5 work nor persisted geometry or data changes.
